            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FOO02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Jesse</forename>
                        <surname>Foot</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1744">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1826"/>
                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Ed Pope notes: Jesse Foot DNB 1744-1826 surgeon. A good example of how
                            Godwin varied spelling of names randomly. Notes: Boyle's 1800 listed a
                            John Foote esq of 79 Wimpole St and Charlton Place nr Canterbury. Another
                            possible was Henry Foote will PCC 1843 picture dealer St Marylebone. He
                            had four brothers who were surgeons (John of Bloomsbury and Covent Garden
                            PCC 1839, William of Edgware PCC 1844, Charles and Peter both of Gibraltar
                            in 1840). Their father was perhaps John Foote PCC 1797.</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
